{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502887-character-creation-for-more-advanced-mages-m-taw-2e","id":1502887,"title":"Character creation for more advanced mages (M:tAw 2e)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-12T16:01:49-08:00","id":1502887,"title":"Character creation for more advanced mages (M:tAw 2e)","content":"I'm working on a short campaign, and I'm thinking I kind of want most of my characters to start a little bit more advanced than most starting mages. Mebbe give them the option of Adepthood and probably the option of being in a Legacy. In y'all's opinion, what would be a good amount of Experience and Arcane Experience to allow them to spend on their characters before play.<br /> <br /> I could just say &quot;Gnosis 3 and 9 Arcana dots or whatever&quot;, but I kinda like the added flexibility of it being Experience and Arcane Experience. Let them determine in what way they want their characters to be badass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>either e/em/eir pronouns OR fey/fem/fear OR be/bim/bos pronouns {if you don't want to learn new words, singular they is OK}<br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/queermythopoeia\" target=\"_blank\">Support my RPG writing and streaming on Patreon</a>!<br /> <a href=\"https://luciferssubcreations.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Shards: Sub-Creations Taking Root in Ein Soph Aur</a> {an rpg blog}","edited":{"userid":26484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26484-tristissima-et-alia","user":"Tristissima et alia","date":". 02-12-2023, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26484-tristissima-et-alia","name":"Tristissima et alia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T16:16:27-08:00","id":1502888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tristissima et alia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502887-character-creation-for-more-advanced-mages-m-taw-2e#post1502887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm working on a short campaign, and I'm thinking I kind of want most of my characters to start a little bit more advanced than most starting mages. Mebbe give them the option of Adepthood and probably the option of being in a Legacy. In y'all's opinion, what would be a good amount of Experience and Arcane Experience to allow them to spend on their characters before play.<br /> <br /> I could just say &quot;Gnosis 3 and 9 Arcana dots or whatever&quot;, but I kinda like the added flexibility of it being Experience and Arcane Experience. Let them determine in what way they want their characters to be badass.</div> </div> </div> </div>Think is, a more experienced mage could be more experienced on attribute, merits, and skills.<br /> <br /> It is perfectly feasible to have a mage that did not grow much in magical abilities but getting stuff like the Order merits (specially things like Masque and Techne that you can take several times), Order status, Mystery Cult Initiation/Influence, and better stats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T16:23:20-08:00","id":1502890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502887-character-creation-for-more-advanced-mages-m-taw-2e?p=1502888#post1502888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Think is, a more experienced mage could be more experienced on attribute, merits, and skills.<br /> <br /> It is perfectly feasible to have a mage that did not grow much in magical abilities but getting stuff like the Order merits (specially things like Masque and Techne that you can take several times), Order status, Mystery Cult Initiation/Influence, and better stats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes . . . which is why I'm asking how much Experience and Arcane Experience I should give folk at character creation, rather than just giving them more Gnosis and Arcana. So that they can decide that kind of thing. I'm just looking for folks' thoughts on how much Experience and Arcane Experience would be good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>either e/em/eir pronouns OR fey/fem/fear OR be/bim/bos pronouns {if you don't want to learn new words, singular they is OK}<br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/queermythopoeia\" target=\"_blank\">Support my RPG writing and streaming on Patreon</a>!<br /> <a href=\"https://luciferssubcreations.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Shards: Sub-Creations Taking Root in Ein Soph Aur</a> {an rpg blog}","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26484-tristissima-et-alia","name":"Tristissima et alia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T16:30:53-08:00","id":1502892,"title":"","content":"I'd say 10-20xp, maybe? 'S enough to buy a few extra Arcana/Gnosis/Attribute dots, or go heavy into Merits/Skills/Legacies","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T17:26:14-08:00","id":1502899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tristissima et alia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502887-character-creation-for-more-advanced-mages-m-taw-2e#post1502887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm working on a short campaign, and I'm thinking I kind of want most of my characters to start a little bit more advanced than most starting mages. Mebbe give them the option of Adepthood and probably the option of being in a Legacy. In y'all's opinion, what would be a good amount of Experience and Arcane Experience to allow them to spend on their characters before play.<br /> <br /> I could just say &quot;Gnosis 3 and 9 Arcana dots or whatever&quot;, but I kinda like the added flexibility of it being Experience and Arcane Experience. Let them determine in what way they want their characters to be badass.</div> </div> </div> </div>It kind of depends on how much more powerful you want them to be. As a broad rule, I would argue you could use the Elder Creation Rules from THousand Years of Night or the Sumerian Werewolf creating rules from the Forsaken Chronicler's Guide and creatively adapt them over to your needs, and I will point to Mummy the Curse Second Edition giving starting characters 10 EXP to represent some of the experiences they forgot about (arguably 10 EXP nicely fills in for the idea of two to three stories, if that rough rule of thumb helps). Requiem also has suggested EXP for tiers of charater type, and you can probably reasonably make an estimated guess on which one fits your needs in Mage.<br /> <br /> Cauthon's overall suggestion somewhere from 10 to 20 EXP is a good one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T17:34:21-08:00","id":1502902,"title":"","content":"Given my experience with this game I would actually give them two seperate experience point pools, one to be spent on Gnosis and Arcana and one for everything else. My biggest complaint with these games is that you quickly end up with a group of Masters who can't do much else, one trick ponies who tie their shoes with magic because they can't do it any other way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T19:58:54-08:00","id":1502908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502887-character-creation-for-more-advanced-mages-m-taw-2e?p=1502902#post1502902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given my experience with this game I would actually give them two seperate experience point pools, one to be spent on Gnosis and Arcana and one for everything else. My biggest complaint with these games is that you quickly end up with a group of Masters who can't do much else, one trick ponies who tie their shoes with magic because they can't do it any other way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't judge me. Using <u>Telekinesis</u> to tie my shoes is a great workout. How else can I come to understand the subtle interplay of Matter and Forces? /j<br /> <br /> I actually quite like Exalted 3e's take on that - Solar XP <i>explicitly cannot</i> be spent on supernatural stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 02-13-2023, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T20:40:14-08:00","id":1502909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502887-character-creation-for-more-advanced-mages-m-taw-2e?p=1502908#post1502908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't judge me. Using <u>Telekinesis</u> to tie my shoes is a great workout. How else can I come to understand the subtle interplay of Matter and Forces? /s<br /> <br /> I actually quite like Exalted 3e's take on that - Solar XP <i>explicitly cannot</i> be spent on supernatural stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a hard house rule to implement, as is &quot;only so many Arcana can be x, all else be lower.&quot; The natural Gnosis limitations on Arcana is actually your best friend here, as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T21:11:15-08:00","id":1502911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502887-character-creation-for-more-advanced-mages-m-taw-2e?p=1502909#post1502909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not a hard house rule to implement, as is &quot;only so many Arcana can be x, all else be lower.&quot; The natural Gnosis limitations on Arcana is actually your best friend here, as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. As long as it doesn't go into 1e's hard-cap on Arcana known, at any rate. I quite like 2e, the &quot;Solar XP&quot; bit was mostly just a suggestion of how to force some variety out of players who only ever beeline the Arcana/Gnosis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T13:46:32-08:00","id":1502955,"title":"","content":"Becoming a Master is 28XP if you start with a 3 dot arcana (or 23/18 if you they cash in their initial merit dots for Gnosis). So aim somewhat under that if you want them to stick to being adepts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T14:23:31-08:00","id":1502958,"title":"","content":"Again, the simplest solution is to establish a Gnosis limit at 3, maybe 4 if you want multiple adeptness, and then select a moderate amount of EXP. (The OP might try making a few characters of their own to see how they feel about it. Since I need to make a few sample characters, i might put up a what I get from a more fleshed out version of what I have and my own vibe on it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T05:43:12-08:00","id":1503019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502887-character-creation-for-more-advanced-mages-m-taw-2e?p=1502955#post1502955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Becoming a Master is 28XP if you start with a 3 dot arcana (or 23/18 if you they cash in their initial merit dots for Gnosis). So aim somewhat under that if you want them to stick to being adepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or require arcane XP for Gnosis, and given them 9 arcane XP plus ~30 regular XP.<br /> <br /> It depends on what kind of game you want to run, obviously, but you might require only arcane XP for learning Arcana without a tutor. Or similar restrictions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T12:42:28-08:00","id":1503056,"title":"","content":"20 EXP, no Arcane EXP is probably the neatest and cleanest of the answers, going over the numbers.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Well, actually, an elaboration from the OP, if we can: Do you want them to be first-degree adept, or do you want them to be second- or third-degree adepts? (multiple arcana)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-14-2023, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-17T08:31:15-08:00","id":1503318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502887-character-creation-for-more-advanced-mages-m-taw-2e?p=1503056#post1503056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Well, actually, an elaboration from the OP, if we can: Do you want them to be first-degree adept, or do you want them to be second- or third-degree adepts? (multiple arcana)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'd want second-degree Adepthood to be the upper limit ~ possible, but it would mean the player would have had to build the entire character around it, with no other priorities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>either e/em/eir pronouns OR fey/fem/fear OR be/bim/bos pronouns {if you don't want to learn new words, singular they is OK}<br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/queermythopoeia\" target=\"_blank\">Support my RPG writing and streaming on Patreon</a>!<br /> <a href=\"https://luciferssubcreations.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Shards: Sub-Creations Taking Root in Ein Soph Aur</a> {an rpg blog}","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26484-tristissima-et-alia","name":"Tristissima et alia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-17T15:03:41-08:00","id":1503344,"title":"","content":"So a starting character has 10 merit dots and 6 Arcana dots, at least 3 of which must be in their Ruling Arcana. So just follow that as a basis. First you set their starting Gnosis based on the expected power level, which cannot be increased at character creation. Next you give an amount of normal XP that cannot be used to purchase Arcana, then give Arcana dots on top of that. Purchasing above your Gnosis limit costs two dots instead of one. That would mean the rules for generating mages of each tier could look something like:<br /> <br /> <b>Trained in the basics:</b> Same as standard character creation (hereafter referred to as CC)<br /> <b>Basic field experience:</b> Gnosis 2 + CC + 2 Arcana dots + 3 XP<br /> <b>Skilled magus:</b> Gnosis 3 + CC + 4 Arcana dots + 5 XP<br /> <b>Seasoned sorcerer:</b> Gnosis 4 + CC + 5 Arcana dots + 8 XP<br /> <b>Knowledgeable master:</b> Gnosis 5 + CC + 7 Arcana dots + 10 XP<br /> <br /> The idea for a new mage remains mostly the same. Those with a bit more experience can be double Disciples with two dots in something else or broaden their horizons further, with 3 mundane XP being used to show they are acquiring skills or building contacts, but are not quite there yet. When the third tier is reached, you can be a double Adept in your Ruling Arcana or an Adept in a non-Ruling one, depending on how you go about it. The XP value is adjusted to account for continuous progress.<br /> <br /> When Gnosis 4 is reached, something interesting happens your Arcana cap does not go up. So in this case the Arcana dot progression is less than the previous tier jump, but the XP boost is higher, signifying the mage focusing on the skills, knowledge and resources that make them all the more effective in their specialties. Lastly, tier 5 is a powerful boost to showcase the culmination of all the hard work that leads to mastery.<br /> <br /> I think that should help give them the freedom to create anything between very specialized characters and jacks of all trades. Hope it helps !","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-17-2023, 07:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}